<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Túpac Amaru Revolutionary Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1982–1997</span> · Also known as MRTA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupac-amaru">Túpac Amaru</a> Revolutionary Movement (MRTA) was a Marxist–Leninist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> group active in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> from the early 1980s, smaller than and rival to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shining-path">Shining Path</a>. It is best known for seizing the Japanese ambassador's residence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in December 1996 and holding dozens of hostages for four months, until Peruvian commandos stormed the building in April 1997, killing all fourteen rebels. The group never recovered from that defeat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tupac-amaru-revolutionary-movement.jpg" alt="Túpac Amaru Revolutionary Movement" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_MRTA.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
